|F1 raw - F1 norm| at alpha=0.30 (decomposed default): 0.0042
|F1 raw - F1 norm| worst across swept alphas:          0.0407

DECOMPOSED (alpha=0.30): robust to cosine scaling -- the headline
ablation numbers do not depend on the raw-vs-normalized choice; no
change and no re-run needed there.

ALPHA SWEEP: normalizing cosine compresses its range, which shifts
what a given alpha *means* (it makes priority relatively more
influential at the same alpha). So the best-alpha COORDINATE can move
even when the achievable peak F1 is comparable. The substantive
plateau/tradeoff finding is scale-invariant; the specific alpha values
are a convention of the raw-cosine scale used throughout the paper.

